message: "If you use these findings or certificates, please cite this repository."
title: "The 3x3 matrix multiplication tensor: verified findings around rank 23"
authors:
  - name: "RakTikoo"
version: 1.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
license: MIT
keywords:
  - matrix multiplication
  - tensor rank
  - Brent equations
  - Laderman
  - computational algebra
abstract: "Exact Jacobian kernel dimensions at Laderman's and Perminov's rank-23 schemes for the 3x3 matrix multiplication tensor (kernel 76 and 94 over Q; excess over trivial tangents 6 and 24), a covering-parity case split for term-repair instances, five completely decided repair instances, a flip-component census of Perminov's cn122, exact pair-merge exclusions, and a completely decided quarters exclusion (174/174 cases UNSAT) — all with machine-checkable certificates. Version 1.1.0 adds a census showing every unit term in the banked rank-23 schemes is a naive term (41 of 41), kernel measurements at Perminov's cr58_cn122 and at ranks 24 and 26 showing no monotone behaviour in the rank, a bounded cross-family transplant census, and an exact audit of two claims in a January 2026 report. Version 1.2.0 adds an extension of the unit-term census to every other verified scheme on the campaign disk (49 of 50 unit terms naive, with a single rank-24 counterexample, so the universal form does not extend beyond the original bank) and a cluster anatomy of the three rank-23 schemes under one fixed greedy procedure. Version 1.3.0 adds a census of the complete Heule–Kauers–Seidl repository of rank-23 schemes (17,376 schemes, all with entries in {−1, 0, 1}; all 1,882 unit terms naive, no off-support unit term in the population), an anatomy of the campaign's homotopy walks showing their terms-merging trips were anti-parallel cancellation artefacts of an unsigned monitor, the closure of the cross-scheme transplant census at all cardinalities ≤ 4 across the 60-scheme enlarged bank (the only hits are the constructed split's own undoing), and a single-drop delta table over six schemes spanning ranks 23–26 (a wrong=1 neighbour exactly where a unit term exists; the one off-support flavour at proj-24). No rank-22 decomposition is claimed."
